# Data conversion with explicit representation and unit

Verifies `->to(type, unit)` changes both the numeric representation and the unit of a data measure. Forward, converting 1B to 0.001KB and 1.5B to 0.0015KB scales the magnitude and casts it to decimal; backward, converting 1.5KB to 1500B scales by the integer coarser-to-finer ratio and casts the whole decimal magnitude back to integer.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1B
print(forward_whole->to(decimal, KB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5B
print(forward_fractional->to(decimal, KB))
backward_whole: decimal = 1.5KB
print(backward_whole->to(int, B))

<<< stdout
0.001KB
0.0015KB
1500B

<<< stderr
